Sources and derivation
----------------------
The table inventory, freshness values, structural conventions and the SQL
examples cited in this repository are derived from Stripe's public
documentation at https://docs.stripe.com/data/. Table names, column names,
freshness figures and schema relationships are factual observations about a
published interface.

Descriptions, notes, grain statements and caveats in this repository are
original editorial content written by this project's contributors, except for
short quotations that are attributed inline to the Stripe documentation page
they came from (see the `source` and `quote` fields in
sources/conventions.json and the `doc_sources` field on individual columns).

Accuracy
--------
Stripe publishes the authoritative, complete column list only inside the
Sigma schema browser in the Stripe Dashboard. It is not available in any
machine-readable public form. This dataset therefore combines:

  - what Stripe documents publicly (marked `documented`),
  - what follows from conventions Stripe documents (marked `conventional`),
  - curated knowledge that has not been proven against a live account
    (marked `community`).

Treat `community` columns as candidates to verify, not as facts. Run
tools/verify_against_sigma.py against your own Stripe account to confirm them,
and please contribute the results back.

No warranty. Do not use this dataset as the sole basis for financial,
accounting, tax or regulatory reporting without verifying against your own
Stripe data.

Sample data
-----------
All data under dist/samples/ and dist/sigma_sample.sqlite is synthetic, produced
by tools/generate_samples.py. It contains no real Stripe data, no real customer
information, and no real payment credentials. Names, emails and identifiers are
fabricated.

